    "id": "windows-11-10-bsod-memory-management-0x0000001a",
    "title": "How do I resolve Windows 11/10 BSOD MEMORY_MANAGEMENT (0x0000001A)?",
    "question": "How do I resolve Windows 11/10 BSOD MEMORY_MANAGEMENT (0x0000001A)?",
    "directAnswer": "Stop code MEMORY_MANAGEMENT (0x0000001A) points to faulty RAM sticks, unstable XMP/EXPO overclocks, or corrupted page files. Press Win + R, run mdsched.exe (Windows Memory Diagnostic) or boot MemTest86 to test each RAM module individually, disable RAM overclocking in BIOS, update GPU/chipset drivers, and run chkdsk C: /f /r to verify disk integrity.",
