    "content": "<div class=\"ai-direct-answer\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\n    <div class=\"ai-answer-badge\">&#9889; Quick Expert Answer &bull; Windows 11 &amp; Windows 10</div>\n    <p itemprop=\"text\"><code class=\"kb-inline-code\">UNEXPECTED_STORE_EXCEPTION</code> occurs when the Windows kernel store component encounters an I/O failure on an SSD/HDD or conflict with Fast Startup. Disable Fast Startup under <strong>Control Panel &gt; Power Options &gt; Choose what the power buttons do</strong>, update NVMe/SSD firmware via the manufacturer utility, run <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">chkdsk C: /f /r</code>, and check SMART health metrics for failing drive sectors.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4>Step-by-Step Diagnostic &amp; Resolution Protocol</h4>\n\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 1</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Root Cause &amp; Initial Verification</div>\n    <p><code class=\"kb-inline-code\">UNEXPECTED_STORE_EXCEPTION</code> occurs when the Windows kernel store component encounters an I/O failure on an SSD/HDD or conflict with Fast Startup.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 2</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Primary Resolution Procedure</div>\n    <p>Disable Fast Startup under <strong>Control Panel &gt; Power Options &gt; Choose what the power buttons do</strong>, update NVMe/SSD firmware via the manufacturer utility, run <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">chkdsk C: /f /r</code>, and check SMART health metrics for failing drive sectors.</p><div class=\"kb-code-box\">chkdsk C: /f /r</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"kb-warning-box\">\n    <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Expert Safety &amp; Verification Note:</strong> Always back up critical files or create a System Restore point before modifying Windows Registry keys, disk partitions, or BIOS/UEFI firmware settings. Download updates and redistributables exclusively from official Microsoft portals.\n</div>"
