    "directAnswer": "Drives missing in File Explorer often lack an assigned drive letter or have a corrupted partition table. Press Win + X > Disk Management: if the drive shows a healthy partition without a letter, right-click it and select Change Drive Letter and Paths > Add. If it reads RAW, do not format it—run chkdsk X: /f or use read-only recovery software first to protect your data.",
