    "title": "How do I fix Windows 11 Modern Standby battery drain overnight while laptop lid is closed?",
    "question": "How do I fix Windows 11 Modern Standby battery drain overnight while laptop lid is closed?",
    "directAnswer": "Modern Standby (S0 Low Power Idle) keeps Wi-Fi active during sleep, causing laptops to stay warm and drain 30%–50% in a bag. Unplug power *before* closing the lid (a known S0 transition bug), configure Hibernate instead of Sleep for closing the lid on battery in Control Panel > Power Options, and run powercfg /sleepstudy to pinpoint waking devices.",
