    "question": "How do I fix Outlook emails stuck in the Outbox and refusing to send?",
    "directAnswer": "Emails stall in the Outbox when attachments exceed server limits (typically 20–25 MB), Outlook is in Work Offline mode, or you opened the queued message while sending. Click Send/Receive > Work Offline to verify you are online, open Outbox, move the message to Drafts, compress or link large files via OneDrive, and resend.",
