    "content": "<div class=\"ai-direct-answer\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\n    <div class=\"ai-answer-badge\">&#9889; Quick Expert Answer &bull; Microsoft Outlook</div>\n    <p itemprop=\"text\">Broken attachment previews occur when the PDF/Word preview handler is disabled or Protected View conflicts with Adobe/Edge. In Outlook, go to <strong>File &gt; Options &gt; Trust Center &gt; Trust Center Settings &gt; Attachment Handling</strong>, uncheck <strong>Turn off Attachment Preview</strong>, click <strong>Attachment and Document Previewers</strong>, enable the required handlers, and repair Office if Word/Excel previewers still fail.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4>Step-by-Step Diagnostic &amp; Resolution Protocol</h4>\n\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 1</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Root Cause &amp; Initial Verification</div>\n    <p>Broken attachment previews occur when the PDF/Word preview handler is disabled or Protected View conflicts with Adobe/Edge.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 2</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Primary Resolution Procedure</div>\n    <p>In Outlook, go to <strong>File &gt; Options &gt; Trust Center &gt; Trust Center Settings &gt; Attachment Handling</strong>, uncheck <strong>Turn off Attachment Preview</strong>, click <strong>Attachment and Document Previewers</strong>, enable the required handlers, and repair Office if Word/Excel previewers still fail.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"kb-warning-box\">\n    <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Expert Safety &amp; Verification Note:</strong> Always back up critical files or create a System Restore point before modifying Windows Registry keys, disk partitions, or BIOS/UEFI firmware settings. Download updates and redistributables exclusively from official Microsoft portals.\n</div>"
