    "title": "How do I fix \"Excel ran out of resources while attempting to calculate one or more formulas\"?",
    "question": "How do I fix \"Excel ran out of resources while attempting to calculate one or more formulas\"?",
    "directAnswer": "This triggers from volatile formulas (OFFSET, INDIRECT) across whole columns, corrupted formatting in unused million-row cells, or multi-threaded calculation bugs. Press Ctrl + End to locate and delete bloated empty rows/columns, switch File > Options > Formulas > Enable multi-threaded calculation to Manual (1–2 threads) or upgrade from 32-bit to 64-bit Office for large workbooks.",
