    "question": "How do I fix OneDrive \"Your OneDrive is full\" or frozen account even after deleting gigabytes of files?",
    "directAnswer": "Deleted OneDrive files remain counted against your storage quota inside the OneDrive Recycle Bin (and Second-Stage Recycle Bin on business accounts), and Outlook.com attachments share the same Microsoft Storage pool. Sign in to onedrive.live.com, empty Recycle bin, check account.microsoft.com/storage for Outlook attachment usage, and wait up to 2 hours for quota release.",
    "category": "windows",
