    "content": "<div class=\"ai-direct-answer\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\n    <div class=\"ai-answer-badge\">&#9889; Quick Expert Answer &bull; MacBook, iMac &amp; macOS</div>\n    <p itemprop=\"text\">macOS Sequoia's built-in firewall updates and third-party VPN/antivirus network extensions (CrowdStrike, Little Snitch, Norton, Cisco) frequently break DNS resolution after updates. Open <strong>System Settings &gt; Network &gt; Filters</strong> (and <strong>VPN</strong>) to disable stale proxy/content filter extensions, switch DNS to <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">1.1.1.1</code> / <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">8.8.8.8</code>, and flush DNS via <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">sudo dscacheutil -flushcache; sudo killall -HUP mDNSResponder</code>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4>Step-by-Step Diagnostic &amp; Resolution Protocol</h4>\n\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 1</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Root Cause &amp; Initial Verification</div>\n    <p>macOS Sequoia's built-in firewall updates and third-party VPN/antivirus network extensions (CrowdStrike, Little Snitch, Norton, Cisco) frequently break DNS resolution after updates.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 2</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Primary Resolution Procedure</div>\n    <p>Open <strong>System Settings &gt; Network &gt; Filters</strong> (and <strong>VPN</strong>) to disable stale proxy/content filter extensions, switch DNS to <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">1.1.1.1</code> / <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">8.8.8.8</code>, and flush DNS via <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">sudo dscacheutil -flushcache; sudo killall -HUP mDNSResponder</code>.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"kb-warning-box\">\n    <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Expert Safety &amp; Verification Note:</strong> Always verify an up-to-date iCloud or local Finder/iTunes backup before choosing Restore in Recovery Mode, and never enter your Apple Account credentials on third-party unlock websites.\n</div>"
