    "question": "Why does PayPal charge sellers a $20 Chargeback Fee even if the seller wins or refunds?",
    "directAnswer": "When a buyer files a dispute directly with their credit card issuer (an external chargeback) rather than through PayPal's Resolution Center, card networks charge PayPal a dispute processing fee that PayPal passes to the merchant ($20 USD) unless the transaction qualifies in full for PayPal Seller Protection. Issuing a prompt refund when a buyer messages you prevents costly chargeback fees.",
