    "title": "How do I stop Norton Smart Firewall from blocking my home Wi-Fi printer, NAS, or local network shares?",
    "question": "How do I stop Norton Smart Firewall from blocking my home Wi-Fi printer, NAS, or local network shares?",
    "directAnswer": "Norton classifies new Wi-Fi networks as Public (Restricted) by default, which blocks LAN printer discovery and SMB shares. Open Norton 360 > Device Security > Settings > Firewall > Network Trust, find your home Wi-Fi SSID, and change its trust level from Public to Private (or Full Trust), then restart the printer.",
    "category": "antivirus",
    "categoryLabel": "Antivirus & Endpoint Security",
    "subCategory": "Norton 360 & LifeLock",
    "readTime": "3 min read",
