    "directAnswer": "By security design, toggling Real-Time Protection off in Windows Security is strictly temporary—Windows automatically re-enables it after a short interval or upon reboot to protect users from forgetting. Instead of disabling Defender globally, add a targeted File or Folder Exclusion under Virus & threat protection settings > Manage settings > Exclusions for verified safe software.",
