    "content": "<div class=\"ai-direct-answer\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\n    <div class=\"ai-answer-badge\">&#9889; Quick Expert Answer &bull; Admin Locks, Tamper Protection, Group Policy &amp; Registry Restoration</div>\n    <p itemprop=\"text\"><strong>Tamper Protection</strong> intentionally blocks PowerShell and Registry modifications to Defender core settings (<code class=\"kb-inline-code\">DisableRealtimeMonitoring</code>, etc.) even as Administrator! You must either run the change through the Windows Security GUI, temporarily toggle <strong>Tamper Protection OFF</strong> inside Windows Security (for approved admin maintenance), or verify <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">WinDefend</code> is actively running.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4>Step-by-Step Diagnostic &amp; Resolution Protocol</h4>\n\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 1</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Root Cause &amp; Initial Verification</div>\n    <p><strong>Tamper Protection</strong> intentionally blocks PowerShell and Registry modifications to Defender core settings (<code class=\"kb-inline-code\">DisableRealtimeMonitoring</code>, etc.) even as Administrator!</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 2</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Primary Resolution Procedure</div>\n    <p>You must either run the change through the Windows Security GUI, temporarily toggle <strong>Tamper Protection OFF</strong> inside Windows Security (for approved admin maintenance), or verify <code class=\"kb-inline-code\">WinDefend</code> is actively running.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"kb-warning-box\">\n    <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Expert Safety &amp; Verification Note:</strong> Security Advisory: Never disable Real-Time Protection, Tamper Protection, or exclude C:\\ permanently. Before clearing TPM or changing BitLocker/Core Isolation settings, verify your 48-digit BitLocker Recovery Key is saved at account.microsoft.com/devices/recoverykey.\n</div>"
