    "directAnswer": "Windows Exploit Protection's strict memory mitigations occasionally crash older 32-bit applications. Instead of turning off System Settings globally, open Windows Security > App & browser control > Exploit protection settings > Program settings, click Add program to customize, select the specific .exe, and override Control Flow Guard (CFG) to Off solely for that application.",
