    "question": "How do I fix Memory Integrity blocking older Western Digital (wdcsam64_prewin8.sys), Brother, or USB-to-Serial drivers?",
    "directAnswer": "Legacy pre-Windows 10 drivers like wdcsam64_prewin8.sys (WD SES driver), ene.sys (RGB lighting), or old ftdibus.sys lack HVCI code-integrity compliance. Download the latest Windows 11-signed driver from the vendor—or if the peripheral is no longer owned, locate its oemXX.inf name in the Review incompatible drivers dropdown and purge it with pnputil /delete-driver oemXX.inf /uninstall.",
