    "content": "<div class=\"ai-direct-answer\" itemscope itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Answer\">\n    <div class=\"ai-answer-badge\">&#9889; Quick Expert Answer &bull; Core Isolation, Memory Integrity (HVCI), Incompatible Drivers &amp; TPM</div>\n    <p itemprop=\"text\">By Microsoft's strict security design, <strong>Smart App Control</strong> can ONLY be activated on a <strong>clean installation of Windows 11</strong> (it starts in Evaluation Mode and automatically locks permanently to <strong>Off</strong> if your PC was upgraded from Windows 10 or had incompatible unsigned apps during evaluation). Re-enabling Smart App Control requires a clean Windows 11 Reset/reinstall.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h4>Step-by-Step Diagnostic &amp; Resolution Protocol</h4>\n\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 1</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Root Cause &amp; Initial Verification</div>\n    <p>By Microsoft's strict security design, <strong>Smart App Control</strong> can ONLY be activated on a <strong>clean installation of Windows 11</strong> (it starts in Evaluation Mode and automatically locks permanently to <strong>Off</strong> if your PC was upgraded from Windows 10 or had incompatible unsigned apps during evaluation).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"kb-step-box\">\n    <div class=\"kb-step-num\">Step 2</div>\n    <div class=\"kb-step-title\">Primary Resolution Procedure</div>\n    <p>Re-enabling Smart App Control requires a clean Windows 11 Reset/reinstall.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"kb-warning-box\">\n    <strong>&#9888;&#65039; Expert Safety &amp; Verification Note:</strong> Security Advisory: Never disable Real-Time Protection, Tamper Protection, or exclude C:\\ permanently. Before clearing TPM or changing BitLocker/Core Isolation settings, verify your 48-digit BitLocker Recovery Key is saved at account.microsoft.com/devices/recoverykey.\n</div>"
