    "directAnswer": "Windows Defender Firewall creates separate rules for the virtual vEthernet (WSL) network adapter, which often defaults to Public and blocks host-to-WSL traffic. Open elevated PowerShell and inspect Get-NetFirewallProfile / allow the vEthernet (WSL) interface via New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName \"WSL\" -Direction Inbound -InterfaceAlias \"vEthernet (WSL)\" -Action Allow (for trusted local dev ports only).",
    "category": "defender",
